High Priority for 1.0.0 Release:
- Fix button icons in Files browser
- Bug stomping / fixing in Files browser
- Add missing actions to News browser

User Editor:
- Need to check that it works, and polish the UI

General:
- Help feature within GtkHx. It should at least explain available keyboard shortcuts.
- Publish to Flathub
- Keyboard shortcuts like Ctrl-W and Ctrl-Q ought to work in all windows/dialogs including Settings

Icons:
- Support GIF icon extension https://github.com/fogWraith/Hotline/blob/main/Docs/Protocol/GIF-Icons.md

Docs:
- Rewrite README.md to explain this project better
- Write a section about migrating from 0.9.4 to modern versions

i18n:
- Translate to other languages

Security:
- TLS support (see mobius as an example server that supports it; https://github.com/jhalter/mobius/blob/master/docs/tls.md)
  - Also I think Janus supports it?
- Default to encryption on? Can we tell if a server supports encryption? If not, we can try connecting with encryption first, and then fallback to no encryption

Bookmarks:
- Better bookmark management, allowing user to add/edit/delete bookmarks within GtkHx

Tracker:
- Ship with some more built in trackers configured
- New Tracker protocol support

Voice Chat:
- Build initial prototype of voice chat extension https://github.com/fogWraith/Hotline/blob/main/Docs/Protocol/Capabilities-Voice.md

Inline Media:
- Research spike to determine how difficult it would be to add to xtext (see spec https://github.com/fogWraith/Hotline/blob/main/Docs/Protocol/Capabilities-Inline-Media.md)

Code Modernization:
- Better modules with more code reuse
- Define string / resource consts instead of repeating them (or having them littered throughout the code)

Plugins:
- New plugin ABI using GIRepository

Features:
- Ability to make GtkHx themes. These would allow customization of all the buttons in the UI
- Custom color palette
- Log chat history / server, and be able to bring that chat history back up when connecting to a server (separate from chat history extension, could be tricky to handle both of these)
